#. (itstool) path: info/desc
#: C/cpu-multicore.page:16
msgid ""
"Computers with more processors find it easier to run many programs at the "
"same time."
msgstr ""
"Datamaskinar med fleire prosessorar synest det er lettare å køyre mange "
"program samtidig."

#. (itstool) path: page/title
#: C/cpu-multicore.page:19
msgid "Why do I have more than one processor?"
msgstr "Kvifor har eg meir enn éin prosessor?"

#. (itstool) path: page/p
#: C/cpu-multicore.page:21
msgid ""
"Many computers have more than one processor (CPU). These are sometimes "
"referred to as multi-core systems."
msgstr ""
"Mange datamaskinar har meir enn éin prosessor (CPU). Desse vert av og til "
"kalla fleirkjernesystem."

#. (itstool) path: page/p
#: C/cpu-multicore.page:23
msgid ""
"The workload of running all of the programs on your computer is shared "
"between the processors. The more processors you have, the more the work can "
"be shared out. This reduces the load on each processor, which can help make "
"the computer run faster."
msgstr ""
"Arbeidsmengda med å køyre alle appane på datamaskina di vert delt mellom "
"prosessorane. Jo fleire prosessorar du har, dess meir kan arbeidet delast "
"opp. Dette reduserer belastninga på kvar prosessor, noko som kan hjelpe til "
"med å få datamaskina til å køyre raskare."

#. (itstool) path: page/p
#: C/cpu-multicore.page:25
msgid ""
"The computer automatically decides how best to share the work between "
"processors; you don't need to do this yourself."
msgstr ""
"Datamaskina avgjer automatisk korleis arbeidet best kan delast mellom "
"prosessorar; du treng ikkje gjere dette sjølv."

#. (itstool) path: info/desc
#: C/process-many.page:16
msgid "Lots of system processes run automatically in the background."
msgstr "Mange systemprosessar køyrer automatisk i bakgrunnen."

#. (itstool) path: page/title
#: C/process-many.page:19
msgid "Why are there processes listed that I did not start?"
msgstr "Kvifor er det oppførte prosessar som eg ikkje har starta?"

#. (itstool) path: page/p
#: C/process-many.page:21
msgid ""
"There are usually lots of processes listed under the <gui>Processes</gui> "
"tab. Only a few of these will be programs that you started yourself. The "
"others are mostly processes that are needed by the operating system to make "
"the computer run correctly. These are started automatically when you log in, "
"and typically run quietly in the background."
msgstr ""
"Det er vanlegvis mange prosessar som er lista under "
"<gui>Prosessar</gui>-fana. Berre nokre få av desse er program som du sjølv "
"har starta. Dei andre er stort sett prosessar som operativsystemet treng for"
" at datamaskina skal fungere korrekt. Desse vert starta automatisk når du "
"loggar inn, og køyrer typisk stille i bakgrunnen."

#. (itstool) path: info/desc
#: C/process-priority-change.page:19
msgid ""
"Decide whether a process should get a bigger or smaller share of the "
"processor's time."
msgstr ""
"Avgjer om ein prosess skal få ein større eller mindre del av prosessortida."

#. (itstool) path: page/title
#: C/process-priority-change.page:22
msgid "Change the priority of a process"
msgstr "Endre prioriteten til ein prosess"

#. (itstool) path: page/p
#: C/process-priority-change.page:24
msgid ""
"You can tell the computer that certain processes should have a higher "
"priority than others, and so should be given a bigger share of the available "
"computing time. This can make them run faster, but only in certain cases. "
"You can also give a process a <em>lower</em> priority if you think it is "
"taking up too much processing power."
msgstr ""
"Du kan fortelje datamaskina at visse prosessar skal ha høgare prioritet enn "
"andre, og dermed få ein større del av den tilgjengelege reknetyda. Dette kan"
" få dei til å køyre raskare, men berre i visse tilfelle. Du kan også gje ein"
" prosess ein <em>lågare</em> prioritet dersom du meiner han brukar for mykje"
" prosesseringskraft."

#. (itstool) path: item/p
#: C/process-priority-change.page:27
msgid ""
"Go to the <gui>Processes</gui> tab and click on the process you want to have "
"a different priority."
msgstr ""
"Gå til <gui>Prosessar</gui>-fana og klikk på prosessen du vil ha ein annan "
"prioritet."

#. (itstool) path: item/p
#: C/process-priority-change.page:28
msgid ""
"Right-click the process, and use the <gui>Change Priority</gui> menu to "
"assign the process a higher or lower priority."
msgstr ""
"Høgreklikk på prosessen, og bruk <gui>Endre prioritet</gui>-menyen for å "
"tildele prosessen høgare eller lågare prioritet."

#. (itstool) path: page/p
#: C/process-priority-change.page:31
msgid ""
"There is typically little need to change process priorities manually. The "
"computer will usually do a good job of managing them itself. (The system for "
"managing the priority of processes is called <link xref=\"process-priority-"
"what\">nice</link>.)"
msgstr ""
"Det er som regel lite behov for å endre prosessprioritetar manuelt. "
"Datamaskina vil som regel gjere ein god jobb med å styre dei sjølv. "
"(Systemet for å styre prosessprioritet vert kalla <link xref=\"process-"
"priority-what\">nice</link>.)"

#. (itstool) path: section/title
#: C/process-priority-change.page:35
msgid "Does higher priority make a process run faster?"
msgstr "Gjev høgare prioritet ein raskare prosess?"

#. (itstool) path: section/p
#: C/process-priority-change.page:37
msgid ""
"The computer shares its processing time between all of the running "
"processes. This is normally shared intelligently, so programs that are doing "
"more work automatically get a bigger share of the resources. Most of the "
"time, processes will get as much processing time as they need, and so will "
"already be running as fast as possible. Changing their priority won't make a "
"difference."
msgstr ""
"Datamaskina deler prosesseringstida si mellom alle dei køyrande prosessane. "
"Dette vert normalt delt intelligent, slik at appane som gjer meir arbeid "
"automatisk får ein større del av ressursane. Som regel får prosessane så "
"mykje prosesseringstid som dei treng, og vil dermed allereie køyre så fort "
"som mogleg. Å endre prioriteten deira vil ikkje utgjere nokon skilnad."

#. (itstool) path: section/p
#: C/process-priority-change.page:39
msgid ""
"If your computer is running several computationally-intensive programs at "
"once, however, its processing time may be \"over-subscribed\" (that is, the "
"<link xref=\"process-identify-hog\">processor's full capacity</link> will be "
"in use). You may notice that other programs run slower than usual because "
"there is not enough processing time to share between all of them."
msgstr ""
